tem information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta3.mono - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4080 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7602) - AMD Ryzen 7 9800X3D 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 63.62 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nGodot.Collections.Dictionaries that use a Enum as their key, where the Enum is a Byte type enum incorrectly treat their key as signed in inconsistent/unpredictable ways.  In specific, this prevents C# (possibly GDS?) access to keys above 127, and returns incorrect results from .Contains(key)\n\nThis incorrect signed behavior also seems to extend to [Tool] Resources.  But that will go in a second bug report.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSee Minimum reproduction project attached.\n>Run Minimum reproduction project\n>Observe incorrect output in Godot log.\n\nOr more specifically, what the project is doing/reproduction steps regardless of project:\n>Define C# Enum as a byte underlying type\n>Create a Godot Dictionary\n>Add Enum values above 127 to the dictionary.\n>Observe that value addition works correctly, and the VSCode inspector will list the values.\n>Observe that Dictionary.Keys lists the correct enum value keys.\n\n>Attempt to access a key above 127 using index access\n>Observe the thrown exception\n>Attempt Dictionary.Contains() with keys above 127\n>Observe the incorrect (false) result.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[EnumBug Project.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21171621/EnumBug.Project.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url"